  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "16. Actions",
    "ruleNumber": "16.01",
    "summary": "An Action can specify its start and finish points, who qualifies, a use cap, a payoff and extra restrictions. To begin, the unit must be on the battlefield. AIRCRAFT, FORTIFICATION and [Battle-shocked](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock) units are ineligible, as are units with an [Objective Control](vsdata:core-rule/profiles) value of 0 or –. An [Engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) unit needs TITANIC. The unit also loses eligibility for that turn once it has [Advanced](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move), [Fallen Back](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back) or started any Action. From the moment it starts until turn end, the unit cannot declare a charge and only a TITANIC unit can shoot. Departure from the battlefield or movement other than a [Pile-in](vsdata:core-rule/pile-in-move) or [Consolidation](vsdata:core-rule/consolidation-move) prevents completion. Apply the Action's Effect if it finishes.",
